"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible In: 4.5.beta2.official.e1b4101e3\nNot reproducible In: 4.4.1.stable.official.49a5bc7b6\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta2 - macOS Sequoia (15.3.1) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 (Apple7) - Apple M1 (8 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI am trying to setup CI a pipeline for 4.5-beta2 on macOS on an EC2 instance.\n\nWhen I run the Godot 4.5-beta2 binary on macOS in a headless environment (an AWS EC2 instance accessed via SSH) the `--version` command hangs.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```bash\ncurl -LO https://github.com/godotengine/godot-builds/releases/download/4.5-beta2/Godot_v4.5-beta2_macos.universal.zip\nunzip -oq Godot_v4.5-beta2_macos.universal.zip\nmkdir -p ~/godot-4.5-beta2\nmv Godot.app ~/godot-4.5-beta2\ntouch ~/godot-4.5-beta2/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/_sc_\n~/godot-4.5-beta2/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot --version     # <-- THIS HANGS\n```\n\nIf I start a VNC session on the machine and login to the OS GUI as ec2-user and then run the `--version` command in the original SSH session it will work. If I then logout the ec2-user from the macOS GUI then the `--version` command will hang again.\n\nI have also tested:\n\n```bash\n~/godot-4.5-beta2/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot --headless --version    # <--- HANGS\n~/godot-4.5-beta2/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot --embedded --headless --version  # <--- does not hang but has other issues with exporting\n```\n\nThis issue also exists in 4.5-beta1 but not prior Godot versions.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNo MRP - issue happens before opening a project","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://av